# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

An MCP server built with [FastMCP](https://github.com/jlowin/fastmcp), generated from
[mcpserver-template](https://github.com/zerotropism/mcpserver-template) with the `{{ backend }}`
backend. The server only knows the `TaskRepository` protocol; the backend is injected.

## Run

```bash
uv sync --all-groups
uv run pytest
uv run {{ project_slug }}          # serves over stdio
```

## Try it from a client

[mcp-servers-cli](https://pypi.org/project/mcp-servers-cli/) lists what the server exposes and
lets a model drive its tools:

```bash
uvx mcp-servers-cli inspect --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
uvx mcp-servers-cli agent "Add a task: write the report, then list pending tasks" \
  --model qwen3.5:4b-mlx --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
```

`filter_tasks` takes a nested object: small local models struggle with it. See the measured
requirements in the mcp-servers-cli README before picking a model.
{%- if backend == "sqlite" %}

## Storage

Tasks are stored in SQLite, at `DB_PATH` when it is set, otherwise in the per-user data
directory (`platformdirs`), never in the current directory. MCP clients forward only a short
list of environment variables to a stdio server, so pass `DB_PATH` explicitly:

```bash
uvx mcp-servers-cli inspect --env DB_PATH=$PWD/tasks.db --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
```
{%- endif %}

## MCP API

| Kind | Name |
|---|---|
| Tools | `add_task`, `complete_task`, `complete_tasks`, `delete_task`, `filter_tasks` |
| Resources | `tasks://all`, `tasks://pending`, `tasks://completed`, `tasks://stats`, `tasks://today`, `tasks://weekly-summary` |
| Prompts | `task_summary_prompt`, `priority_analysis_prompt`, `scheduling_prompt`, `weekly_review_prompt` |

`filter_tasks` takes one `TaskFilter`; every criterion is optional and they combine with AND:
`{"task_filter": {"status": "pending", "keyword": "report"}}`. Errors are raised as MCP errors;
no tool returns an `{"error": ...}` dictionary.

## Layout

```
src/{{ module_name }}/
├── models.py              Task, TaskFilter, TaskStats
├── repository.py          TaskRepository protocol and TaskNotFoundError
├── repositories/
│   └── {{ backend }}.py          the {{ backend }} backend
└── server.py              tools, resources and prompts; repository injected
tests/                     same contract suite for any backend
```

Adding a backend means one class implementing the protocol's seven methods; the tests in
`tests/test_repositories.py` apply to it unchanged once the `repo` fixture builds it.

## Keeping up with the template

The answers given at generation are in `.copier-answers.yml`. To bring in a newer version of
the template:

```bash
uvx copier update
```

Commit `uv.lock` after the first `uv sync`: Dependabot needs it to propose updates.
